<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<table><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Public methods</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Construction</td><td><code>New()</code>, <code>NewDefaults()</code>, <code>WithDefaults()</code>, <code>FromFS(fsys, lock)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Packages</td><td><code>WithPackages</code>, <code>WithPackage</code></td></tr><tr><td>Provider and logging</td><td><code>WithProvider</code>, <code>WithLogger</code></td></tr><tr><td>Directories</td><td><code>RootDir</code>, <code>CacheDir</code>, <code>AssetsDir</code></td></tr><tr><td>Preparation</td><td><code>CacheOrFetch(ctx)</code>, <code>Fetch(ctx)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Vendoring</td><td><code>Vendor(ctx, dir)</code>, <code>VendorLocal(dir)</code>, <code>ReadLock(fsys, name)</code>, <code>LockFile</code>; the types <code>Lock</code>, <code>LockedPackage</code> and <code>LockedFile</code></td></tr><tr><td>Map entries</td><td><code>WithImport</code>, <code>WithFile</code>, <code>WithVersionedPaths</code>, <code>ModulePreload</code></td></tr><tr><td>URLs and serving</td><td><code>URL</code>, <code>WithURLFunc</code>, <code>WithAssets</code>, <code>Manifest</code>, <code>ServeFile</code></td></tr><tr><td>Head and tags</td><td><code>Render</code>, <code>RenderWith</code>, <code>RenderWithHash</code>, <code>WithRenderOptions</code>, <code>Styles</code>, <code>Script</code>, <code>Stylesheet</code>, <code>FuncMap</code></td></tr><tr><td>Render options</td><td><code>WithIntegrity</code>, <code>WithStableIntegrity</code>, <code>WithNonce</code></td></tr><tr><td>Content-Security-Policy</td><td><code>ScriptHash</code>, <code>RenderWithHash</code></td></tr><tr><td>JSON</td><td><code>Imports</code>, <code>ImportsIndent</code>, <code>Scopes</code>, <code>Marshal</code>, <code>MarshalIndent</code></td></tr><tr><td>Shim</td><td><code>ShimPath</code>, <code>Shim</code></td></tr><tr><td>Cleanup</td><td><code>Clean</code></td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Defaults</h2>
<p><code>NewDefaults</code> configures cdnjs, <code>.importmap</code> and <code>assets</code>; it loads no module shim. <code>New</code> creates an empty structure; configure the provider, cache and asset directories yourself before preparing packages. <code>FromFS</code> starts from <code>New</code> with the fingerprints of its file system, so it needs no provider or directories; its URLs begin with <code>/assets/</code> unless <code>WithURLFunc</code> sets them.</p>
<h2>Package and provider types</h2>
<p><code>library.Package</code> declares name, version, required files, an optional provider, <code>License</code> (the licence text <code>Vendor</code> copies) and <code>Local</code> (files the application builds itself). <code>library.Includes</code> contains <code>library.Include</code> selections with <code>File</code>, <code>As</code> and <code>Raw</code>. A <code>library.Provider</code> returns <code>library.Files</code> and the resolved version for a package request.</p>
<h2>The assets package</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Identifier</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>assets.Fingerprint(fsys, opts...)</code>, <code>MustFingerprint</code></td><td>A <code>*Manifest</code> with the SHA-384 of every file that is not hidden; <code>Only(files...)</code> limits it to those files, <code>Reload()</code> fingerprints again when files change</td></tr><tr><td><code>URL</code>, <code>PlainURL</code>, <code>Version</code>, <code>Integrity</code>, <code>TagIntegrity</code></td><td>A file's address with and without its version, the version, and its Subresource Integrity; <code>TagIntegrity</code> is empty while the manifest reloads</td></tr><tr><td><code>ServeFile</code></td><td>Serving with a strong <code>ETag</code>; the current version may be cached for a year</td></tr><tr><td><code>Stylesheet</code></td><td>A stylesheet tag for a file with its versioned URL and integrity (none while the manifest reloads); an unknown file is an error</td></tr><tr><td><code>Files</code>, <code>Has</code>, <code>Reloads</code>, <code>WithURLFunc</code></td><td>The fingerprinted files, whether one is known, whether the manifest reloads, and how its addresses are made</td></tr><tr><td><code>assets.Integrity(data)</code>, <code>Versioned(url, version)</code>, <code>ScriptTag</code>, <code>StylesheetTag</code></td><td>Helpers for data and addresses of your own</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>The importmap command</h2>
<pre><code>importmap vendor [-config importmap.json] [-out assets/vendor] [-timeout 2m] [-local]
importmap verify [-out assets/vendor] [-root dir]</code></pre>
<p>The command lives in <code>github.com/donseba/go-importmap/cmd/importmap</code>; <a href="{{ basePath }}/vendoring" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/vendoring" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">vendoring</a> describes its configuration and the lock file.</p>
<h2>Error handling</h2>
<p>Preparation and output methods return errors; most configuration methods return the instance for chaining. <code>FromFS</code> returns an error for a lock it cannot read and for a listed file that is missing or does not match its integrity. <code>Clean</code> removes configured directories and returns the instance rather than exposing deletion errors.</p>
<p><a href="https://github.com/donseba/go-importmap/tree/v1.5.0">Browse the v1.5.0 source and provider adapters</a> for the exact signatures.</p>
</article>
